- op: discuss  # 2638
  at: '2026-06-28T20:25:20Z'  # 2638
  by: agent  # 2638
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2638
  clock: 12  # 2638
  nonce: '2638'  # 2638
  message: "SATISFIED — all three symptoms fixed (symptoms 1&2 PR e70e2ef759; symptom 3 PR 6f78430878, human-ruled A=yes/B=yes/C=yes). Behavioral evidence, fresh hypergumbo run on packages/hypergumbo-core/src:\n\nSymptom 3 (collection mutators -> mutate, not write): mutator-method call edges (.append/.add/.extend/.insert/.setdefault/.update) = 757 access_mode='mutate', 6 'read' (the 6 are mutator-named calls on an assignment RHS, correctly read), 0 still mislabeled 'write' (was: all 'write'). python.yaml library_patterns now maps the in-place mutators to `mutate`; .write/.send/.put stay `write` (external-sink writes, decision B); .pop/.remove/.clear/.discard/.popitem stay `delete` (decision C).\n\nSymptoms 1&2 (read-evidence -> read, not write), from the earlier verify: references self-contradiction 2082->0, module_attr_ref 531->0.\n\nThe four-cell read/write/mutate/delete vocabulary is now used as intended (overall self-corpus distribution read 5141 / mutate 1054 / write 72 / delete 16) instead of `write` being overloaded with both reads and mutations. The invariant statement (\"access-mode values derived from evidence type or call target; reads labeled read, collection mutations labeled mutate, only true assignments labeled write; two metadata fields on the same edge that encode the same property must agree\") now holds. Production-path tests: dataflow read-evidence override (TestAnnotateDataflowAst) + the real-python.yaml mutator mapping (TestMutatorAccessModePythonYaml)."  # 2638
- op: discuss  # 48a8
